 152:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****         /* Allocate the event group.  Justification for MISRA deviation as
 153:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * follows:  pvPortMalloc() always ensures returned memory blocks are
 154:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * aligned per the requirements of the MCU stack.  In this case
 155:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * pvPortMalloc() must return a pointer that is guaranteed to meet the
 156:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * alignment requirements of the EventGroup_t structure - which (if you
 157:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * follow it through) is the alignment requirements of the TickType_t type
 158:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * (EventBits_t being of TickType_t itself).  Therefore, whenever the
 159:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * stack alignment requirements are greater than or equal to the
 160:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * TickType_t alignment requirements the cast is safe.  In other cases,
 161:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * where the natural word size of the architecture is less than
 162:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * sizeof( TickType_t ), the TickType_t variables will be accessed in two
 163:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * or more reads operations, and the alignment requirements is only that
 164:Middlewares/FreeRTOS/Source/event_groups.c ****          * of each individual read. */
